  "statement": {
    "title": "The torch.nn child-replacement API mishandles top-level and strict requests",
    "body": "The torch.nn child-replacement API mishandles a single-name target and provides no way to distinguish create-or-replace from replace-only behavior. A non-strict call must create or replace a child under an existing parent, a strict call must reject a missing child, and both top-level and dotted targets must reject values that are not neural-network components.",
